extract_result.scope:
a. This DR applies to all USDA Mission Areas, agencies, staff offices, programs, teams, organizations, appointees, and employees, including contractors and grantees receiving Federal funds that utilize and collect geospatial data. This policy introduces the geospatial data management objectives for the implementation of the GDA for the adoption of geospatial data management best practices, used by USDA internal and external geospatial data creators, partners, publishers, and consumers.
b. This DR applies to USDA’s geospatial portfolio, including all geospatial data created for, by, and enhanced by USDA, with a priority focus on the USDA’s National Geospatial Data Assets (NGDA), other data supporting NGDA data theme communities and NSDI, and other Geospatial Authoritative Data (GAD). GAD is any geospatial data that meets one or more of the following:
(1) Is defined by statute;
(2) Is authored, maintained, and considered authoritative by USDA Mission Areas, agencies, and staff offices;
(3) Is used to support policy;
(4) Is used to manage programs; or
(5) Is used to inform the public.
c. The USDA geospatial data will include geospatial standards processes to ensure data integrity throughout the lifecycle, including the acquisition, storage, and distribution process.
d. Authoritative data products used in emergency response situations will have established data lifecycle controls before and after emergency deployments. During emergency response execution, the USDA Geospatial Information Officer (GIO) will defer to Mission Area, agency, and staff office discretion in the determination of the characteristics of authoritative data products.
